{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RB5JG8mJhBYMSeTj2YkEFM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper (14 pages) and the review context YAML. Let me summarize what I know:\n\n**Paper**: \"When Does Cross-Lingual Calibration Transfer Work? Geometric Analysis and Practical Solutions\"\n- Studies cross-lingual correctness probe transfer across 2 MoE architectures (Qwen3-235B, Llama 4 Scout), 20 languages, 3 resource tiers\n- Key findings: (1) depth-transferability Pareto frontier is architecture-dependent, (2) CaCLR (MMD-based) is a systematic negative result, (3) ~30% low-resource probing results are artifacts, (4) linear projection with ~70 pairs is practical recommendation, (5) Procrustes effect reversal at ~0.55 threshold\n\n\n- Camera-ready version adds Gemma 4 31B as a third architecture and expands to 52 languages\n\nThe target venue appears to be EACL based on the guidance notes, though the paper doesn't explicitly state this. I need to look up the appropriate reviewer guidelines and then assign reviewers—one focused on methods and experiments, another on novelty and related work—before running the full review. I'll dispatch both reviewers in parallel to speed up the process, then move into the roundtable discussion, and finally compile the report.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5276,"cache_read_input_tokens":61377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5276},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91a2196c-7a23-4294-80ba-646c05703e7b","uuid":"3e511484-69c4-40b8-be22-245d9c6e71c9"}
