o consult the full ARR reviewer guidelines document directly at aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines, as the search results only show partial content from that page.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91a2196c-7a23-4294-80ba-646c05703e7b","uuid":"9619105b-3289-4c0b-ad50-9813e67e4154","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:58:47.950Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL ARR reviewer guidelines scoring criteria 1-5 scale 2025 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Q6rowaBnWasAATHVrCcBJF","content":[{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about ARR reviewer guidelines for 2025-2026:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. \n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific details about the 1-5 scale definitions or the detailed scoring criteria for each of these three dimensions. 