{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01255ANAnMLeWZi3pmeyZJHk","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"papers:\\\\n  miao2026closing:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Closing the Confidence-Faithfulness Gap in Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Ruoxi Miao\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Lyle Ungar\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.25052\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Showed correctness direction and verbalized confidence direction are orthogonal (cosine < 0.04) in 7-8B models. Motivates probing internal representations. English-only — our cross-lingual extension is the natural next step.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  xiao2025knowledge:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Analyzing LLMs' Knowledge Boundary Cognition Across Languages Through the Lens of Internal Representations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Zheng Xiao\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ACL 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.13816\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"cross_lingual_probing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Closest prior work. Cross-lingual transfer of knowledge-boundary probes (answerable vs unanswerable). Key differences: they probe knowledge boundaries (input-level), we probe correctness (output-dependent); they measure probing accuracy, not ECE/Brier; they test 8 languages, we target 20+.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  civelli2026shared:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"A Shared Geometry of Difficulty in Multilingual Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Andrea Civelli\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.12731\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"cross_lingual_probing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Cross-lingual difficulty probe transfer at intermediate layers. Architecture-dependent optimal depth (24-49%). Probes IRT difficulty (question property), not correctness (model property). Critical control for our difficulty ablation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  zhou2025lace:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Beyond the Final Layer: Intermediate Representations for Better Multilingual Calibration in LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Zhou\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.03136\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"multilingual_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"LACE: adaptive layer ensemble for multilingual calibration. Confirmed 5x ECE gap across 100+ languages. Requires per-language validation data. Our CaCLR needs no non-English correctness labels.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  ravisankar2026dali:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Can you map it to English? The Role of Cross-Lingual Alignment in Multilingual Performance of LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Ravisankar\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EACL 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.09378\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"cross_lingual_alignment\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"DALI: causal evidence via activation patching that English middle-layer representations fix non-English errors across 24 languages. Strongest causal support for our hypothesis.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  miao2026coral:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Correctness-Optimized Residual Activation Lens (CORAL)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Ruoxi Miao\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.06022\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Transferable correctness probes via regularized MLP on residual activations, ~50% ECE improvement at 53-66% depth. English-only, cross-task. CaCLR positioned as solution to their identified distribution-shift transfer degradation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  joshi2025calibration:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Calibration Across Layers: Understanding Calibration Evolution in LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Joshi\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Identified low-dimensional calibration direction in residual stream evolving across layers.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  confidence_manifold2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"The Confidence Manifold: Geometric Structure of Correctness Representations in Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: []\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.08159\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Correctness signals occupy 3-8 dimensions, linearly separable. 25 labeled examples achieve 89% of full-data accuracy. All English-only.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  karandikar2021sbece:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Soft Calibration Objectives for Neural Networks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Archit Karandikar\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nicholas Cain\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Dustin Tran\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Balaji Lakshminarayanan\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Jonathon Shlens\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Michael C. Mozer\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Becca Roelofs\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2021\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2021\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper/2021/hash/f8905bd3df64ace64a68e154ba72f24c-Abstract.html\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"calibration_foundations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"SB-ECE: differentiable soft-binned ECE enabling gradient-based calibration optimization. Core component of our CaCLR objective.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  khanmohammadi2025ccps:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Calibrating LLM Confidence by Probing Perturbed Representation Stability (CCPS)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Khanmohammadi\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.21772\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Calibration via probing perturbed representation stability at final layer. ~55% ECE reduction. English-only, single layer. No cross-lingual or multi-layer analysis.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  liu2025middle:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Middle-Layer Representation Alignment for Cross-Lingual Transfer in Fine-Tuned LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Liu\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Niehues\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ACL 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"cross_lingual_alignment\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Middle layers form strongest language-agnostic shared space. Supports our hypothesis about intermediate-layer transfer.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  ji2025calibrating:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Calibrating Verbal Uncertainty as a Linear Feature to Reduce Hallucinations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Ji\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Verbal uncertainty governed by single linear direction in representation space.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  bendavid2010theory:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"A Theory of Learning from Different Domains\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Shai Ben-David\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"John Blitzer\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Koby Crammer\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Alex Kulesza\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Fernando Pereira\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Jennifer Wortman Vaughan\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2010\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Machine Learning, Vol. 79, pp. 151-175\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10994-009-5152-4\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"domain_adaptation_theory\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"H-divergence framework for domain adaptation. Theoretical basis for bounding target error via source error and domain divergence — underpins our cross-lingual transfer analysis.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  zhao2019invariant:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"On Learning Invariant Representations for Domain Adaptation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Han Zhao\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Remi Tachet des Combes\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Kun Zhang\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Geoffrey J. Gordon\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2019\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v97/zhao19a.html\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"domain_adaptation_theory\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Proves marginal distribution matching fails when conditional distributions differ. Motivates why naive cross-lingual probe transfer may degrade — our CaCLR addresses this gap.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  zhang2019bridging:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Bridging Theory and Algorithm for Domain Adaptation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Yuchen Zhang\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Tianle Liu\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Mingsheng Long\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Michael I. Jordan\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2019\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v97/zhang19i.html\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"domain_adaptation_theory\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Margin Disparity Discrepancy — tighter generalization bound connecting domain adaptation theory to practical adversarial algorithms. Complements Ben-David and Zhao theoretical foundations.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  hewitt2019control:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Designing and Interpreting Probes with Control Tasks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"John Hewitt\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Percy Liang\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2019\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://aclanthology.org/D19-1275/\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"probing_methodology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Defines selectivity metric for probes — ensures probe accuracy reflects encoded information, not classifier capacity. Methodological baseline for our probing evaluation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  voita2020mdl:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Information-Theoretic Probing with Minimum Description Length\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Elena Voita\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Ivan Titov\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2020\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2020\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.14/\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"probing_methodology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"MDL probing — information-theoretic alternative measuring compression quality rather than raw accuracy. More robust evaluation metric for cross-lingual probe transfer.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  belinkov2022probing:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Probing Classifiers: Promises, Shortcomings, and Advances\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Yonatan Belinkov\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2022\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Computational Linguistics, Vol. 48, No. 1, pp. 207-219\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://aclanthology.org/2022.cl-1.7/\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"probing_methodology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Comprehensive survey of probing methodology — defines best practices, pitfalls, and evaluation standards we follow in our experimental design.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  kornblith2019cka:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Similarity of Neural Network Representations Revisited\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Simon Kornblith\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Mohammad Norouzi\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Honglak Lee\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Geoffrey Hinton\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2019\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v97/kornblith19a.html\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"representation_similarity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Centered Kernel Alignment (CKA) — our primary metric for measuring cross-lingual representation similarity across layers.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  wu2020similarity:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Similarity Analysis of Contextual Word Representation Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"John Wu\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Yonatan Belinkov\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Hassan Sajjad\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nadir Durrani\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Fahim Dalvi\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"James Glass\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2020\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ACL 2020\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.422/\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"representation_similarity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Applies CKA and SVCCA to compare contextual word representations across architectures — direct precedent for our cross-lingual representation similarity analysis.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  guo2017calibration:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"On Calibration of Modern Neural Networks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Chuan Guo\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Geoff Pleiss\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Yu Sun\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Kilian Q. Weinberger\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2017\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2017\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v70/guo17a.html\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"calibration_foundations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Temperature scaling baseline — canonical post-hoc calibration method we compare against. Established ECE as standard calibration metric.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  angelopoulos2023conformal:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Conformal Prediction: A Gentle Introduction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Anastasios N. Angelopoulos\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Stephen Bates\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2023\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Foundations and Trends in Machine Learning, Vol. 16, No. 4, pp. 494-591\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://www.nowpublishers.com/article/Details/MAL-101\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"calibration_foundations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Distribution-free uncertainty quantification framework — theoretical grounding for our conformal prediction extension of CaCLR.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\ncategories:\\\\n  mechanistic_calibration: \\\\\\\"Probing/steering calibration signals in LLM internal representations\\\\\\\"\\\\n  cross_lingual_probing: \\\\\\\"Cross-lingual transfer of probes/directions in multilingual models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  cross_lingual_alignment: \\\\\\\"Language alignment and shared representations in multilingual LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n  multilingual_calibration: \\\\\\\"Calibration methods for multilingual LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n  calibration_methods: \\\\\\\"General calibration objectives and techniques\\\\\\\"\\\\n  domain_adaptation_theory: \\\\\\\"Theoretical foundations for domain adaptation and representation learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  probing_methodology: \\\\\\\"Methodology for probing neural network representations\\\\\\\"\\\\n  representation_similarity: \\\\\\\"Metrics and methods for comparing neural network representations\\\\\\\"\\\\n  calibration_foundations: \\\\\\\"Foundational calibration and uncertainty quantification methods\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nmeta:\\\\n  created_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n  last_updated: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21\\\\\\\"\\\\n  total_papers: 22\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 13373, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01V11DrQuXXH7sDRR266jaVy","session_id":"91a2196c-7a23-4294-80ba-646c05703e7b","uuid":"5b849530-3312-4a84-bb8a-46cdb96bd62e","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:01:03.115Z"}
