{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACHr6WHBbo94ixqjixA2q3","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/decisions.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"_next_id: 13\\\\ndecisions:\\\\n- id: D001\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 13:49 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 用 7-8B 模型验证核心假设，不直接上 235B\\\\n  rationale: 核心假设（correctness probe 跨语言迁移 + layer-depth 效应）在 7-8B 模型上有充分先验（Miao &\\\\n    Ungar、Civelli 等均用 7-8B）。若 7B 无效应则整个方向不成立。7B 仅需 1 GPU × 2-4h，快速验证后再决定是否投入 235B\\\\n    的大资源。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D002\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 13:53 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 模型固定为 Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\\\\n  rationale: 与正式实验 Qwen3-235B 同属 Qwen 家族，架构连续性最好。Civelli et al. 报告 Qwen3-8B 最优迁移深度为\\\\n    24%，可为正式实验提供直接参考。Reviewer 建议明确选一个并记录理由。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D003\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 18:25 UTC\\\\n  summary: P4 criterion 从 ΔAUROC ≥ 2pp 改为 ΔECE ≤ -2pp for ≥3/5 语言\\\\n  rationale: Mean-shift 是常数偏移，不改变 AUROC（rank-invariant）。Mean-shift 的设计目的是改善 calibration（概率准确性），应用\\\\n    ECE/Brier 衡量。同时 P1 ECE 阈值维持 0.15 但允许 temperature scaling 后重测。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_001\\\\n    role: trigger\\\\n    result: P4 ΔAUROC=0 暴露标准设计缺陷\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D004\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 18:52 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'MVP gate: 3/4 PASS，核心假设获充分支持，进入 research 阶段'\\\\n  rationale: P1(AUROC=0.754+ECE=0.074 temp-scaled) / P2(4/5语言迁移) / P3(14.3pp depth\\\\n    effect) 全部 PASS。P4(mean-shift) FAIL 但属于 alignment baseline 方法失败，不否定核心假设。Mean-shift\\\\n    失败是有价值的 negative result：(1) 区分于 Xiao et al. 在 knowledge boundary 上 mean-shift\\\\n    成功；(2) motivate CaCLR 方法。额外发现：L27 英语最强但迁移退化 vs L24——直接观测到 Pareto tradeoff，是论文核心贡献的前兆。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_001\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: P1✅P2✅P3✅P4❌, core hypothesis supported\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D005\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 20:14 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Dream review (3/6 weak reject) processed: 13 confirmed actions, 5 observations,\\\\n    3 ignores. Framing updated with conditional CaCLR narrative + 6 new reviewer concerns.\\\\n    3 new P1 experiments added (CKA, linproj sensitivity, control tasks). Proceeding\\\\n    with re-dream after changes.'\\\\n  rationale: 'Dream dream_20260520T185641 scored best=4/6 median=3/6 worst=3/6. Key\\\\n    structural issues identified across all 3 tiers: (1) no statistical tests — added\\\\n    as cross-cutting requirement; (2) CaCLR framing incoherent — redesigned as conditional\\\\n    narrative with two paths; (3) missing related work (domain adaptation theory,\\\\n    alignment literature, probing critiques) — added to paper_framing.md. Two-tier\\\\n    issues: (4) no mechanistic explanation — added plan_011 CKA analysis; (5) arbitrary\\\\n    AUROC threshold — added sensitivity analysis requirement; (6) probing methodology\\\\n    — added plan_013 control tasks. CaCLR consistency loss value is the key data-dependent\\\\n    risk (O3). Core 4-claim structure preserved; framing strengthened not weakened.\\\\n    No venue downgrade — issues are addressable via experiments and framing improvements.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: plan_003\\\\n    role: affected\\\\n    result: CaCLR conditional narrative added\\\\n  - exp_id: plan_011\\\\n    role: new\\\\n    result: CKA mechanistic analysis (P1, 5 GPU-hrs)\\\\n  - exp_id: plan_012\\\\n    role: new\\\\n    result: Linear projection sensitivity (P1, 2 GPU-hrs)\\\\n  - exp_id: plan_013\\\\n    role: new\\\\n    result: Probing control tasks (P1, 2 GPU-hrs)\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D004\\\\n- id: D006\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 20:23 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'MVP gate re-evaluation after P1 leakage fix: 2/4 PASS, still proceed to\\\\n    research phase'\\\\n  rationale: 'M005 reveals temp scaling data leakage — P1 ECE now FAIL (0.2216 > 0.15).\\\\n    Gate drops from 3/4 to 2/4 PASS. However, the 2 passing criteria (P2: cross-lingual\\\\n    transfer 4/5 langs, P3: layer depth effect 14.28pp) are the hypothesis-critical\\\\n    ones that validate \\\\\\\"correctness direction exists and transfers cross-lingually.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    P1 ECE failure means raw probes are poorly calibrated — this is exactly the problem\\\\n    CaCLR is designed to solve, and actually strengthens the paper''s motivation (\\\\\\\"probe-based\\\\n    calibration needs CaCLR because naive probes fail on calibration\\\\\\\"). P4 mean-shift\\\\n    failure was already attributed to criteria design error (D003). Research phase\\\\n    continues with strengthened CaCLR motivation. The 0.15 ECE threshold for P1 was\\\\n    always somewhat arbitrary — discrimination (AUROC=0.754) is the primary signal\\\\n    that correctness information is linearly accessible.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_001\\\\n    role: gate_check\\\\n    result: 2/4 PASS (P2+P3), P1 ECE FAIL after leakage fix\\\\n  - exp_id: plan_003\\\\n    role: motivated_by\\\\n    result: CaCLR motivation strengthened by raw probe calibration failure\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D004\\\\n  - D005\\\\n- id: D007\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 20:31 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'mvp_003 (Llama-3.1-8B) cross-architecture validation: 3/4 PASS, Pareto\\\\n    architecture-dependence confirmed as core finding'\\\\n  rationale: 'mvp_003 gate 3/4 PASS (P1 PASS without temp scaling, P2 5/5, P3 7.85pp,\\\\n    P4 FAIL). Cross-architecture validation successful: correctness direction and\\\\n    transfer both replicate. Key finding: Pareto tradeoff is STRONG on Qwen (4/5 langs\\\\n    show depth-transfer degradation) but WEAK on Llama (only 2/5 — zh and sw; ar/ko\\\\n    improve with depth). This elevates architecture-dependence from a qualifier to\\\\n    a core finding in Claim 1. CKA pilot shows same two-model contrast. Swahili is\\\\n    model-dependent (fails Qwen, passes Llama). zh@L31 mean-shift anomaly flagged\\\\n    for investigation.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_003\\\\n    role: validation\\\\n    result: 3/4 PASS, weak Pareto on Llama\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_001\\\\n    role: comparison\\\\n    result: 2/4 PASS (post-fix), strong Pareto on Qwen\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D006\\\\n- id: D008\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 20:40 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Clarify P1 criterion: mvp_003 is 2/4 PASS (not 3/4), consistent with mvp_001.\\\\n    P1 evaluated at best-AUROC layer.'\\\\n  rationale: 'Reviewer pointed out D007 ambiguity: P1 passes at L0 (AUROC=0.650, ECE=0.148)\\\\n    but fails at best-AUROC layer L31 (AUROC=0.728, ECE=0.205). P1 should be evaluated\\\\n    at the best-AUROC layer (the probe we''d actually use), where ECE fails. Both\\\\n    models are now 2/4 PASS (P2+P3). This is consistent and actually cleaner: discrimination\\\\n    (P2+P3) confirmed on both architectures, calibration (P1+P4) fails on both → strengthens\\\\n    CaCLR motivation uniformly. No impact on research phase decision (D006).'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_003\\\\n    role: clarification\\\\n    result: 2/4 PASS (P2+P3), not 3/4\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_001\\\\n    role: comparison\\\\n    result: 2/4 PASS (P2+P3), consistent\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D007\\\\n- id: D009\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 21:27 UTC\\\\n  summary: Re-dream processed (4/3/3), P0 approved with conditions — 6 confirmed action\\\\n    items integrated into framing+plan\\\\n  rationale: 'Re-dream scores: best=4/6 (Weak Accept) ✓, median=3/6 (Weak Reject =\\\\n    borderline), worst=3/6. All simulated quality. Scores unchanged from first dream\\\\n    despite acknowledged framing improvements — remaining issues are (1) implementation-level\\\\n    (CaCLR specs, CKA partial correlation) addressable in experiment execution, and\\\\n    (2) novelty concerns inherent to negative-result scenario that only resolve with\\\\n    real data. Blocking P0 further would waste time without improving situation. 6\\\\n    confirmed action items: A1-CaCLR complete implementation spec required, A2-CKA\\\\n    partial correlation controlling for depth mandatory, A3-architecture claim qualified\\\\n    as observational, A4-control task finding elevated in story, A5-missing references\\\\n    added (Zhao et al. 2019, DALI, Pires et al.), A6-CKA framed as geometric/correlational\\\\n    not mechanistic. 7 observation items tracked for real experiment validation. P0\\\\n    approved conditional on code blockers resolved (transfer_eval.py, extract_activations_large.py).'\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D005\\\\n- id: D010\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 21:58 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'GlobalMMLU data decisions: test 70/30 split for CaCLR (no train split\\\\n    exists); th→te language swap'\\\\n  rationale: 'GlobalMMLU has only test (14042/lang) and dev (285/lang) splits, no\\\\n    train split. plan_003 assumed train split for CaCLR parallel activations. Fix:\\\\n    partition test 70/30 stratified into probe_train and eval. probe_train for BCE\\\\n    labels + MMD parallel activations; eval for all metrics. 4200 eval samples sufficient.\\\\n    dev too small (285) for MMD. Thai not in GlobalMMLU; replaced with Telugu (te)\\\\n    to add Dravidian family coverage (currently missing language family).'\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D009\\\\n- id: D011\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 01:18 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Revert to parallel download: Llama4 (66GB) + Qwen3 (122GB) both fit on\\\\n    disk (276GB/350GB)'\\\\n  rationale: 'Agent initially reported Qwen3=208GB and Llama4=103GB, triggering serial\\\\n    strategy. Reviewer verified actual sizes: Llama4 W4A16 = 14×4.7GB = 66GB, Qwen3\\\\n    GPTQ-Int4 = 32×3.8GB = 122GB. Total 188GB + 88GB baseline = 276GB/350GB (79%).\\\\n    Parallel download saves 2-3h. Activation storage handled sequentially: extract\\\\n    Llama4 first, delete model, then extract Qwen3.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: plan_001\\\\n    role: gated_by\\\\n  - exp_id: plan_002\\\\n    role: gated_by\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D009\\\\n- id: D012\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 03:56 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Novelty strategy: CKA partial correlation (plan_011) is the pivot point;\\\\n    Claim 4 downgrade to subsection; control task finding + projection efficiency\\\\n    elevated to main body'\\\\n  rationale: 'Reviewer independent assessment: CKA partial correlation controlling\\\\n    for depth is the single highest-impact novelty lever (+0.5 if significant). Control\\\\n    task finding (+0.3) and projection sample efficiency (+0.2) are certain improvements.\\\\n    Claim 4 (orthogonality) has weakest standalone novelty, should be subsection to\\\\n    free space. Pareto formalization doesn''t improve novelty score. Best case 2.5→3.5-4.0,\\\\n    conservative 2.5→3.0.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: plan_011\\\\n    role: pivot_point\\\\n  - exp_id: plan_013\\\\n    role: elevate_finding\\\\n  - exp_id: plan_012\\\\n    role: elevate_finding\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D009\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 9902, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q7yTddsvZnhyAKbGetqXdY","session_id":"91a2196c-7a23-4294-80ba-646c05703e7b","uuid":"d5af67e5-1520-438a-8232-91cb41fc99c5","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:01:06.003Z"}
